Livestock, eggs, milk, and honey (@farming-livestock: 0, is #chapter, #contains @farming-animal-plan, #contains @farming-animal-health, #contains @farming-animal-feed, #contains @farming-animal-products, #contains @gallus-gallus-domesticus, #contains @meleagris-gallopavo, #contains @coturnix-japonica, #contains @bos-taurus, #contains @capra-hircus, #contains @sus-scrofa-domesticus, #contains @ovis-aries, #contains @oryctolagus-cuniculus, #contains @apis-mellifera, #farming-practice @apis-mellifera, #farming-practice @bos-taurus, #farming-practice @capra-hircus, #farming-practice @coturnix-japonica, #farming-practice @farming-animal-feed, #farming-practice @farming-animal-health, #farming-practice @farming-animal-plan, #farming-practice @farming-animal-products, #farming-practice @gallus-gallus-domesticus, #farming-practice @meleagris-gallopavo, #farming-practice @oryctolagus-cuniculus, #farming-practice @ovis-aries, #farming-practice @sus-scrofa-domesticus) { r_7JQED5KAHXM0SXKETE4G4WN7B3
Keep animals only after feed, water, housing, daily care, veterinary access, manure handling, and the product's processing route are arranged. Plants can wait for a better season; dependent animals need care every day.

Chicken, turkey, quail, cattle, goats, pigs, and honey connect to Nutrients.lingua. Sheep and rabbits are additional husbandry examples; no equivalent nutrient entry is implied.
